1. PRIVACY POLICY\par
\line
\par
{\b 1.1 THE SHORT VERSION}\par
Rekzora is an offline-first application. We collect nothing. We track\par
nobody. We phone no home. There is no account, no login, no cloud, no\par
analytics and no advertising of any kind inside Rekzora.\par
\par
{\b 1.2 WHAT DATA REKZORA STORES, AND WHERE}\par
All user data produced by Rekzora stays on YOUR computer, in two places:\par
\par
a) Your Recordings\par
Video files (WebM) you create are saved to the folder YOU choose\par
(by default the "Rekzora Recordings" folder in your Videos library).\par
We never upload, transmit or copy these files anywhere. Only you,\par
or apps you explicitly drop/share them into, can move them off\par
your machine.\par
\par
b) Application Preferences\par
A small local settings file and a recordings index are stored in\par
your own Windows AppData profile folder\par
(C:\\Users\\<you>\\AppData\\Roaming\\Rekzora\\).\par
This holds your theme, frame rate, quality, hotkeys, save folder\par
and thumbnail metadata so the app remembers your setup. It never\par
leaves your device unless Windows Backup or you copy it.\par
Interrupted recordings are additionally kept as temporary files in\par
the same folder tree (Rekzora\\recordings-tmp) together with a small\par
manifest, so Rekzora can offer them to you on the next launch\par
(recovery). They stay on your device until you keep or delete them,\par
or until the app finds an empty temp file with no matching data\par
(then it cleans that pair quietly).\par
\par
{\b 1.3 WHAT WE DO NOT COLLECT}\par
- No personal information (name, address, contact details)\par
- No audio, video or screen content (it is never streamed, uploaded,\par
or processed outside your device memory)\par
- No crash dumps are transmitted automatically\par
- No telemetry, analytics, statistics, or usage tracking of any kind\par
- No cookies, fingerprinting, or advertising identifiers\par
- No purchase/billing data (Rekzora has no paid accounts)\par
\par
{\b 1.4 NETWORK ACCESS}\par
Rekzora does not create or require network connections as part of normal\par
operation. The only networking that can ever occur is initiated and\par
performed BY YOU, outside Rekzora's code ? for example when you click a\par
link that opens your browser, or when you choose to transmit a video\par
using YOUR installed sharing applications (Google Quick Share, SHAREit,\par
LocalSend, Send Anywhere, Xender, Telegram, etc.). When you use those\par
applications you are subject to THEIR privacy policies, not ours.\par
\par
{\b 1.5 MICROPHONE, CAMERA AND SCREEN}\par
Rekzora can only use your microphone, webcam and screen-faces-captured\par
content while a recording is actively running, and only when you (or\par
your recorded hotkey) started it. Windows may display recording\par
indicators during that time. Recordings are written straight to disk;\par
Rekzora does not keep hidden copies.\par
\par
{\b 1.6 CHILDREN}\par
Rekzora is a generic desktop utility and is not directed at children\par
under 13. Because no data is collected, no data about children exists.\par
\par
{\b 1.7 YOUR RIGHTS & DATA DELETION}\par
Because all data already lives on your own device, you are always in\par
full control:\par
- Uninstalling Rekzora (or deleting the portable ZIP/exe) removes the\par
program. Delete the recordings folder to erase recordings.\par
- "Delete recordings from disk" inside Rekzora permanently erases the\par
selected videos from your drive (no recycle bin).\par
- Ticking "Delete my Rekzora data when uninstalling" (where shown) also\par
removes preferences from AppData.\par
\par
{\b 1.8 CHANGES TO THIS POLICY}\par
If this policy ever changes (e.g. an optional update checker is added),\par
changes will be listed here and flagged inside the app before any new\par
behavior activates. No change will silently start collecting data.\par
